---
description: How to use the sdlc-rig SDLC assistant in this repository
alwaysApply: false
---

This repository uses `sdlc` (built on githubnext/rig) for SDLC steps. Reports are written to `.sdlc/reports/` as Markdown and JSON.

- Requirements → `npx sdlc stories "<idea>"`
- Design → `npx sdlc plan "<feature>"` (reads stories.json when present)
- Code review → `npx sdlc review [--base main]`
- Tests → `npx sdlc test [--cmd "<command>"]`
- Security → `npx sdlc security [--compliance HIPAA]`
- Release notes → `npx sdlc release [--from <tag>]`
- Everything before a PR → `npx sdlc pr --base main`

When running inside Cursor, pass `--engine cursor` so the agents use the Cursor CLI and this account's models.
Treat report findings as suggestions: verify against the code before changing anything, and ask before applying edits.
Never echo secrets from reports or diffs.
